From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Plaid Pi <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Nov 2026 00:50:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ext4: mballoc: handle NULL from __filemap_get_folio() on 6.1.y

6.1.191 backported the mballoc page-to-folio conversion (upstream
99b150d84e49 "ext4: convert bd_bitmap_page to bd_bitmap_folio" and
5eea586b47f0 "ext4: convert bd_buddy_page to bd_buddy_folio") as a
dependency of bdc56a9c46b2 ("ext4: fix e4b bitmap inconsistency
reports", CVE-2026-45942). That code tests IS_ERR(folio) after
__filemap_get_folio(), but on 6.1.y __filemap_get_folio() still returns
NULL on a miss (ERR_PTR(-ENOENT) only since 6.4, 66dabbb65d67). A
buddy-bitmap page-cache miss, i.e. any allocation after the page was
reclaimed under memory pressure, therefore dereferences NULL:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0
  pc : folio_test_uptodate+0x0/0x1c
  lr : ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp+0x148/0x32c
  Call trace: ext4_mb_load_buddy ext4_mb_regular_allocator
    ext4_mb_new_blocks ext4_ext_map_blocks ext4_map_blocks ext4_getblk
    ext4_bread ext4_append make_indexed_dir ext4_add_entry ext4_create

(Orange Pi 5B, 6.1.191, eight parallel compilers on a 16 GB board.)
The same conversion was tried in 6.1.167-rc1 and reported there with
the same oops (i.MX6 32-bit and arm64, bisected to the bd_bitmap_folio
commit) before being dropped.

Treat NULL like an error pointer at every __filemap_get_folio() site in
mballoc.c and return -ENOMEM for it, the value the pre-folio code
returned when find_or_create_page() failed.

Not for upstream mainline (ERR_PTR semantics there); 6.1.y only.

Assisted-by: LLM

diff --git a/fs/ext4/mballoc.c b/fs/ext4/mballoc.c
index e77d56c533c0b..cc15907b8a039 100644
--- a/fs/ext4/mballoc.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/mballoc.c
@@ -1375,8 +1375,8 @@ static int ext4_mb_get_buddy_page_lock(struct super_block *sb,
 	poff = block % blocks_per_page;
 	folio = __filemap_get_folio(inode->i_mapping, pnum,
 			FGP_LOCK | FGP_ACCESSED | FGP_CREAT, gfp);
-	if (IS_ERR(folio))
-		return PTR_ERR(folio);
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio))
+		return folio ? PTR_ERR(folio) : -ENOMEM;
 	BUG_ON(folio->mapping != inode->i_mapping);
 	e4b->bd_bitmap_folio = folio;
 	e4b->bd_bitmap = folio_address(folio) + (poff * sb->s_blocksize);
@@ -1389,8 +1389,8 @@ static int ext4_mb_get_buddy_page_lock(struct super_block *sb,
 	/* blocks_per_page == 1, hence we need another page for the buddy */
 	folio = __filemap_get_folio(inode->i_mapping, block + 1,
 			FGP_LOCK | FGP_ACCESSED | FGP_CREAT, gfp);
-	if (IS_ERR(folio))
-		return PTR_ERR(folio);
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio))
+		return folio ? PTR_ERR(folio) : -ENOMEM;
 	BUG_ON(folio->mapping != inode->i_mapping);
 	e4b->bd_buddy_folio = folio;
 	return 0;
@@ -1533,7 +1533,7 @@ ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp(struct super_block *sb, ext4_group_t group,
 
 	/* Avoid locking the folio in the fast path ... */
 	folio = __filemap_get_folio(inode->i_mapping, pnum, FGP_ACCESSED, 0);
-	if (IS_ERR(folio) || !folio_test_uptodate(folio) || folio_test_locked(folio)) {
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio) || !folio_test_uptodate(folio) || folio_test_locked(folio)) {
 		/*
 		 * folio_test_locked is employed to detect ongoing folio
 		 * migrations, since concurrent migrations can lead to
@@ -1543,11 +1543,11 @@ ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp(struct super_block *sb, ext4_group_t group,
 		 * try to get the folio with lock in both cases to avoid
 		 * concurrency.
 		 */
-		if (!IS_ERR(folio))
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio))
 			folio_put(folio);
 		folio = __filemap_get_folio(inode->i_mapping, pnum,
 				FGP_LOCK | FGP_ACCESSED | FGP_CREAT, gfp);
-		if (!IS_ERR(folio)) {
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio)) {
 			if (WARN_RATELIMIT(folio->mapping != inode->i_mapping,
 	"ext4: bitmap's mapping != inode->i_mapping\n")) {
 				/* should never happen */
@@ -1567,8 +1567,8 @@ ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp(struct super_block *sb, ext4_group_t group,
 			folio_unlock(folio);
 		}
 	}
-	if (IS_ERR(folio)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(folio);
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio)) {
+		ret = folio ? PTR_ERR(folio) : -ENOMEM;
 		goto err;
 	}
 	if (!folio_test_uptodate(folio)) {
@@ -1585,12 +1585,12 @@ ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp(struct super_block *sb, ext4_group_t group,
 	poff = block % blocks_per_page;
 
 	folio = __filemap_get_folio(inode->i_mapping, pnum, FGP_ACCESSED, 0);
-	if (IS_ERR(folio) || !folio_test_uptodate(folio) || folio_test_locked(folio)) {
-		if (!IS_ERR(folio))
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio) || !folio_test_uptodate(folio) || folio_test_locked(folio)) {
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio))
 			folio_put(folio);
 		folio = __filemap_get_folio(inode->i_mapping, pnum,
 				FGP_LOCK | FGP_ACCESSED | FGP_CREAT, gfp);
-		if (!IS_ERR(folio)) {
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio)) {
 			if (WARN_RATELIMIT(folio->mapping != inode->i_mapping,
 	"ext4: buddy bitmap's mapping != inode->i_mapping\n")) {
 				/* should never happen */
@@ -1609,8 +1609,8 @@ ext4_mb_load_buddy_gfp(struct super_block *sb, ext4_group_t group,
 			folio_unlock(folio);
 		}
 	}
-	if (IS_ERR(folio)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(folio);
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio)) {
+		ret = folio ? PTR_ERR(folio) : -ENOMEM;
 		goto err;
 	}
 	if (!folio_test_uptodate(folio)) {
